course: dictionary
lesson: 15773
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they give clues. «Before the band played, Sam clipped the tuner onto his guitar.» Clipping something onto a guitar sounds like a tool, so tuner must mean a device here.
explain: «The tuner came on Monday to make the piano sound right.» Here a tuner is a person. The clue is that someone came to do a job. A piano tuner visits to fix the sound of the instrument. Ask yourself: is this a thing or a person? The sentence tells you.
explain: «Dad turned the radio's tuner until the football match came in clearly.» A radio tuner is the part that picks up one station. The clues are radio and station. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "the part of the radio that picks up the station" make sense? If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: Tuner is a noun. A tuner can be a thing or a person.
fact: A tuner can be a device that shows whether a note is too high, too low or just right.
fact: A tuner can be the part of a radio or TV that picks up a chosen station or channel.
fact: A tuner can be a person whose job is tuning instruments, especially pianos.
fact: «Tune» means to adjust an instrument so each note is right, and «tuner» is the word for the device or person who does it.
exercise: «Before the band played, Sam clipped the tuner onto his guitar.» What is a tuner here? | A person who plays the guitar in a band | *A device that shows whether a note is too high, too low or just right | A stage light | A small bag for guitar picks
exercise: «Turn the tuner until the weather report comes in clearly.» What does tuner mean here? | A person who fixes pianos | *The part of a radio that picks up a chosen station | A note that is too high | A kind of microphone stand
exercise: «The tuner came on Monday to make the piano sound right.» Who is the tuner? | *A person whose job is tuning instruments | A shop that sells pianos | A pupil learning the piano | A piano made of wood
test: «The guitarist checked the tuner before she played the first chord.» What is the tuner? | The part of a radio that finds a station | A bag for carrying the guitar | *A device that shows if a note is right | A person who checks the guitar strings for dust
test: «The old tuner spent all morning making every key ring true.» Who is the tuner? | A tool for cutting wood | A device that clips onto a violin | *A person who tunes pianos | A radio part that finds stations
exam: «Mum said the tuner was broken, so the radio kept jumping between stations.» What does tuner mean in this sentence? | A piano tuner who visits the house | A device that clips onto a guitar | *The part of a radio that picks up a chosen station | A person who repairs radios
